  // ============================================================
  // ELEMENT: Osmium (Os, Z=76)
  // UFF LJ. Highest bulk modulus (462 GPa, lowest compressibility) and generally considered the densest naturally occurring element (22.59 g/cm^3, though the Os-vs-Ir density ranking is itself a genuinely contested measurement question in the literature -- both fall within each other's uncertainty bars depending on method, flagged rather than presented as a clean fact). One of the rarest elements in Earth's crust.
  // magnetic susceptibility and speed of sound are estimates, not directly sourced this pass.
